Question: 4 - Student Marks Management — Linear Collection

A teacher does not know the number of students in advance. Student marks need to be stored dynamically.
Question

Write a Java program using an ArrayList to:
•	Store marks. 
•	Display marks. 
•	Find the highest mark. 
•	Calculate the average.
give the java code corretly

import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        ArrayList<Integer> marks = new ArrayList<>();

        // Number of students
        int n = sc.nextInt();

        // Store marks
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int mark = sc.nextInt();
            marks.add(mark);
        }

        // Display marks
        System.out.println("Marks:");
        for (int mark : marks) {
            System.out.println(mark);
        }

        // Find highest mark
        int highest = marks.get(0);

        for (int mark : marks) {
            if (mark > highest) {
                highest = mark;
            }
        }

        // Calculate average
        int sum = 0;

        for (int mark : marks) {
            sum += mark;
        }

        double average = (double) sum / marks.size();

        // Display results
        System.out.println("Highest Mark: " + highest);
        System.out.printf("Average: %.2f%n", average);

        sc.close();
    }
}
